{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/903579-the-world-you-live-in","id":903579,"title":"The World You Live In","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-30T08:54:15-07:00","id":903579,"title":"The World You Live In","content":"I'm curious who ran a campaign in the B&amp;S premade domains, how that went and how you filled in the blanks?<br /> Who/what is the Nameless in your chronicle? What happens when a Ventrue in Bejing embraces three times? Does Berlin ever solve its whatever-it-is problem? Inquiring minds want to know.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Freelance Author and Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","name":"mistress of whispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T07:50:05-07:00","id":904146,"title":"","content":"I'm not running a game IN one of those places, but i am using some of those backgrounds and characters (the setting of my campaigns kind of breaks the game).<br /> <br /> I decided that the nameless was a strix (duh, easy option, I know). Basically, the native vampires of Montreal wanted the french kindred gone and so, through a ritual since forgotten, they contacted the ancient strix in their shadow realm. They struck a bargain and received an regular sized black egg. This was a sort of anchor that allowed a powerful strix, The Nameless to cross into the hulan world. The ancient strix had a plan and the egg was more than it seemed. It maintaints a sort of passage to the shadow realm that reacts to the presence of vampires.Without enough vampires around, the passage would collapse and Nameless would be send back to the shadow realm, but the more vampires are around the egg, the larger the passage. Nameless would do his job and help chase the french kindred, but then, it was to ensure that the vampire population was to increase until it would reach the point where more strix could cross, and in a more premanent way (the egg would hatch).<br /> <br /> Thing is, Nameless, once it had chased the colonists, started to think differently. After all, while powerful, it was only a servant among it's ancient peers (one of whom I decided would be Hantu waiting to come back to the human world as a big badass monster strix). Instead of going through with the original plan, it could just manage the local kindred population so it would be the only strix around and be the uncontested master of it's very own little kingdom. So it did and eventually came up with the rules. The egg is hidden under the cross. At this point, if its plan ever failed, either because not enough kindred would be around anymore, or too many, nameless would send back to its realm or the other strix would emerge and it would be mercilessly devoured either way, the prospect of which is starting to erode its mind. Nameless works its hardest so that local vampires are terrified of it but micromanaging so many things in the city and ensuring the careful culling of the kindred is an exhausting task. Nameless is still powerful, but it is starting to slip a little and grows more and more restless and scared of what would happen if the vampires somehow managed to disrupt the balance it carefuly worked on all these years. The few native ventrue who have an idea of what is at stake realize a massive arrival of ancient strix would be the end of Montreal's kindred, probably even the whole province's.<br /> <br /> <br /> Berlin's Prince is not in Berlin anymore for reasons, now heading a kindred mercenary organization for other kindred to pay for. This is basically so his troups stay in shape in Case Abaddon finds where they are. I never got around to deciding what Abaddon should be and I didn't really find a suitable splat. Didn't want it to be yet another strix. I guess maybe some really messed up spirit could work or a true fae since either of those can be pretty much anything you want them to be. I dunno. This won't have time to come up in my game, though, so whatever.<br /> <br /> <br /> My campaign has a bit of a cyberpunk feel, so of course the Zaibatsu are around. They were eventually booted out of tokyo and ended up where the game takes place, where they act as a kind of megacorp rival power to the prince's government. The Maeda trains and hires security personnel for a price, Ume House does divination and stuff and provides ritualists to the security forces and Takahashi does business and tech. Because I think it's a lot of fun fun, The Takahashi has started outfitting kindred with bionic implants (which is technically possible since you can use willpower to not heal some things, allowing for plastic surgery with the night doctor surgery merit). Of course, since kindred are dead, the implants don't respond to nerve signals. Instead, since vampires can control the blood inside their body, a series of pressure sensitive sensors allow the implants activation and manipulation (although this requires some training and you can't do it when you've completely run out of vitae). So far, the implants have included a retractable blade inside the forearm and taser-like implants in the palm of thehand that cause spasms in other kindred's muscles and give temporary penalties to defense. Implants need power to work (they have a limited number of uses before needing to be recharged depending on the type) and if they're broken, you need an engineer to fix them. So far, it's pretty much more trouble than it's worth, but Takahashi hopes it will learn from it and design better stuff eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}